    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1611">

                <pb facs="1273" n="1263" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1263"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">102.22/8–249: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">McConaughy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-08-02T19:00:00+08:00">August 2, 1949—7
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 2—8:45 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2990. Siege ConGen building lifted 5:50 p. m. August 2nd Local Standard Time on
                    order General Labor Union following second session <pb facs="1274" n="1264"
                        xml:id="pg1264"/> with Thomas and Smith this afternoon. Last unauthorized
                    person has left building and outer gate secured. Besieged officers going home
                    for first time since July 29. ConGen plans to open for normal business tomorrow.
                    For details settlement proposed to Navy by General Labor Union, see AstALUSNA
                    telegram to CNO 020940Z.<anchor n="36" xml:id="d1611-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>ComMarianas, please pass to Ambassador Stuart.<anchor n="37" xml:id="d1611-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent Department, repeated Nanking 1670, Canton 936, Peiping 235.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">McConaughy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1611-f1" n="36" xml:id="d1611-f1-content">
                <p>Not found in Department of the State files.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1611-f2" n="37" xml:id="d1611-f2-content">
                <p>Ambassador Stuart was en route to the United States.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
